---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import '../styles/r3.css';
import { links } from '../data/links';
import { impactCases, specialties } from '../data/portfolio';
---
<MainLayout
  title="Technology | Corrine J Blackthorn"
  description="Explore Corrine J. Blackthorn's work in cybersecurity, identity governance, access management, automation, and security architecture."
>
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="kicker">Cybersecurity and identity governance</span>
        <h1>Architecture starts with understanding the whole system.</h1>
        <p>Identity is where people, technology, risk, and accountability meet. I approach identity and access management by understanding the lifecycle of an account, the purpose of an entitlement, the dependencies behind a control, and the people who rely on it.</p>
        <p>My background spans identity engineering, governance, security, systems operations, automation, and audit readiness. I believe a security program should be measurable and sustainable without becoming unnecessarily difficult to operate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="section-actions">
        <a class="button dark" href="/experience/">Experience and resume</a>
        <a class="button" href={links.personal.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connect professionally</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section section-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">Specializations</span><h2>Access, governance, systems, and trust.</h2><p>Technical depth matters, but so does connecting the decisions across a larger environment.</p></div>
      <div class="grid">
        {specialties.map(area => <article class="card compact-card"><h3>{area.title}</h3><p>{area.description}</p></article>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">Selected professional work</span><h2>What the work looks like in practice.</h2><p>These public examples focus on the problem, approach, and outcome. They deliberately omit confidential employer and implementation details.</p></div>
      <div class="case-study-grid">
        {impactCases.map(item => (
          <article class="card case-study">
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <div><strong>The challenge</strong><p>{item.problem}</p></div>
            <div><strong>The approach</strong><p>{item.approach}</p></div>
            <div><strong>The result</strong><p>{item.result}</p></div>
            <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Related specialties">{item.tags.map(tag => <li>{tag}</li>)}</ul>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="quote-band"><div class="container"><blockquote>Security should be understandable, evidence-based, and usable by the people responsible for it.</blockquote></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="container split">
    <div><span class="kicker">Technical collaboration</span><h2>Systems thinking without losing the human perspective.</h2><p>I am interested in meaningful challenges in identity governance, cybersecurity architecture, access controls, and the systems that support accountability. I value clear documentation, constructive technical debate, and solutions teams can maintain long after a project ends.</p></div>
    <article class="card compact-card"><h3>Explore further</h3><p>Learn more about my experience and the work that shaped it, or visit TechNerd for the broader technical practice.</p><div class="section-actions"><a class="button dark" href="/experience/">Professional experience</a><a class="button" href={links.ventures.techNerd} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechNerd</a></div></article>
  </div></section>
</MainLayout>
